# Engines

outfit "Small Graviton Thruster"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91011
	"cost" 12000000
	thumbnail "outfit/small quarg thruster"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"engine capacity" -50
	"thrust" 80
	"thrusting energy" 5.6
	"thrusting heat" 1.5
	"reverse thrust" 40
	"reverse thrusting energy" 2.8
	"reverse thrusting heat" .75
	"force protection" 0.1
	"inertia reduction" 0.1
	"flare sprite" "effect/graviton flare/graviton flare"
		"frame rate" 5
		"scale" .75
	description "How exactly Quarg thrusters work is unknown, but the mechanism that powers even this small set of engines consumes more energy than some human warships. Where all this energy goes is a complete mystery."
	description "	These engines also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships equipped with them accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."

outfit "Small Graviton Steering"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91010
	"cost" 9000000
	thumbnail "outfit/small quarg steering"
	"mass" 30
	"outfit space" -30
	"engine capacity" -30
	"turn" 1200
	"turning energy" 2.4
	"turning heat" .75
	"force protection" 0.1
	"inertia reduction" 0.1
	description "Despite their small size, these Quarg steering engines can turn their ships on a dime. It is rumored that, unlike human steering thrusters, the Quarg do not care where on the hull these are installed, producing the same rotational moment even if directly in line with the ship's center of mass."
	description "	They also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships with these engines accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."


outfit "Medium Graviton Thruster"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91021
	"cost" 20000000
	thumbnail "outfit/medium quarg thruster"
	"mass" 70
	"outfit space" -70
	"engine capacity" -70
	"thrust" 120
	"thrusting energy" 8
	"thrusting heat" 2
	"reverse thrust" 60
	"reverse thrusting energy" 4
	"reverse thrusting heat" 1
	"force protection" 0.15
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	"flare sprite" "effect/graviton flare/graviton flare"
		"frame rate" 5
	description "Quarg thrusters are quite powerful for their size and produce very little heat, but at the cost of consuming immense amounts of energy. The mechanism by which they produce thrust is unknown, but it is rumored that the passing of a Quarg ship wreaks havoc on every gravitational wave antenna in the system."
	description "	They also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships with these engines accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."


outfit "Medium Graviton Steering"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91020
	"cost" 16000000
	thumbnail "outfit/medium quarg steering"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"engine capacity" -50
	"turn" 2400
	"turning energy" 4
	"turning heat" 1
	"force protection" 0.15
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	description "According to rumor, some Quarg ships have their steering engines installed internally, with no need for external thrusters. Much like a gyroscope, they can seemingly orient a ship from anywhere, but unlike them they never seem to saturate or become locked."
	description "	They also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships with these engines accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."


outfit "Large Graviton Thruster"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91031
	"cost" 32000000
	thumbnail "outfit/large quarg thruster"
	"mass" 100
	"outfit space" -100
	"engine capacity" -100
	"thrust" 185
	"thrusting energy" 12
	"thrusting heat" 3
	"reverse thrust" 92.5
	"reverse thrusting energy" 6
	"reverse thrusting heat" 1.5
	"force protection" 0.2
	"inertia reduction" 0.2
	"flare sprite" "effect/graviton flare/graviton flare"
		"frame rate" 5
		"scale" 1.25
	description "This large set of Quarg thrusters is both powerful and subtle, leaving behind no bright exhaust trail nor emitting any detectable radiation aside from a faint violet glow. This is juxtaposed with the extreme amount of energy these engines consume, enough to power entire stations."
	description "	They also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships with these engines accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."


outfit "Large Graviton Steering"
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 91030
	"cost" 25000000
	thumbnail "outfit/large quarg steering"
	"mass" 70
	"outfit space" -70
	"engine capacity" -70
	"turn" 3600
	"turning energy" 6
	"turning heat" 1.5
	"force protection" 0.2
	"inertia reduction" 0.2
	description "Quarg ships are famed for their ability to turn quickly and precisely, as though oriented by a divine hand rather than the flickering exhaust of human steering thrusters. According to some guesses on their mode of operation, this may be closer to the truth than not."
	description "	They also have strange capabilities which seem to violate the laws of physics as humanity understands them. Ships with these engines accelerate faster under their own power than one would expect, while also taking less impact from external forces."

# Power

outfit "Quantum Vacuum Battery"
	category "Power"
	series "Batteries"
	index 91010
	cost 3000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg quantum battery"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"energy capacity" 60000
	"active cooling" 25
	"cooling energy" 1.25
	description "Human engineers who first came into contact with the Quarg were astonished by the sheer energy density of their technology. This Quarg battery holds enough energy to level a small city, rumored to be stored in the negative quantum vacuum pressure between innumerable tiny plates. Somehow, the battery chills itself as energy is drained from it, seemingly in defiance of the human understanding of thermodynamics."


outfit "Antimatter Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91010
	cost 20000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg antimatter core"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"energy generation" 12
	"heat generation" 10
	description "Although humanity is now capable of producing antimatter in relatively significant quantities when compared to a thousand years ago, it is still nothing next to the output of the Quarg, who can produce enough antimatter to outfit even civilian ships with an extremely compact Antimatter Core. This device releases extreme amounts of energy in a simple, elegant package, all while producing surprisingly little waste heat."


outfit "Singularity Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91020
	cost 50000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg singularity core"
	"mass" 400
	"outfit space" -80
	"energy generation" 23.5
	"heat generation" 22.5
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	description "According to little more than vague allusions by the Quarg, these generators contain a minuscule black hole, spewing radiation as it is fed a trickle of mass. This black hole is small enough to output a truly staggering amount of energy via Hawking radiation, which grows in power as a black hole shrinks, something that suggests the black hole within the Singularity Core is truly microscopic."
	description "	Further wild guesses by scientists and conspiracy theorists alike allege that the Quarg are able to somehow trick the laws of physics themselves to make this black hole weigh far less than it otherwise should, bringing its mass from that of a small moon to something a ship could have a hope of moving."


outfit "Quasar Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91030
	cost 100000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg quasar core"
	"mass" 600
	"outfit space" -120
	"energy generation" 37.5
	"heat generation" 35
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	description "This larger generator appears similar to the Singularity Core, only even more powerful. Little is known about its exact function, but purely based on its name, some have speculated that the Quasar Core's increased output is the result of the black hole at its core being fed enough mass to form a small accretion disk, releasing light and heat as it falls towards the event horizon and is compressed to an unimaginable degree."
	description "	While this process should be far less fuel-efficient than simply capturing the Hawking radiation emitted by the black hole alone, the staggering power density of this generator appears to be evidence it was worth the trade."


